       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you're taking responsibility for it, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any indication where it would be appropriate. The extra dose adds risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and there's no added benefit, because analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below this.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum,** such as 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or whatever you prefer up to that limit.\n- **Add a note to the order** if you want to document the indication or monitoring plan.\n\nIf you still think this dose is needed, for example on advice from a specialist or a protocol I'm not aware of, it should go through your hospital's standard process. That means entering it directly in the order system and having pharmacy review it, so someone with full chart access can verify it.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the in-range options?"
